          { h: "我要一个牛肉面。", p: "Wǒ yào yí ge niúròu miàn.", e: "I want one beef noodle.", k: "okay", tag: "grammar", r: ["一碗牛肉面，好嘞！", "Yì wǎn niúròu miàn, hǎo lei!", "One bowl of beef noodles, coming up!"], note: "个 ge is the catch-all measure word, so she understood. Noodles come in bowls though: 一碗 yì wǎn.", fix: ["我要一碗牛肉面。", "Wǒ yào yì wǎn niúròu miàn."] },
          { h: "我是牛肉面。", p: "Wǒ shì niúròu miàn.", e: "I am beef noodles.", k: "wrong", tag: "grammar", r: ["哈哈，你是牛肉面？你要牛肉面吧？", "Hāha, nǐ shì niúròu miàn? Nǐ yào niúròu miàn ba?", "Haha, you ARE beef noodles? You mean you want beef noodles?"], note: "是 shì links two things that are the same: \"I am beef noodles.\" In English \"I'm the beef noodles\" works when ordering. In Chinese you need 要 yào, want.", fix: ["我要一碗牛肉面。", "Wǒ yào yì wǎn niúròu miàn."] }
